# Install to /etc/sudoers.d/pool-deploy (mode 0440, root:root).
# Two narrow, password-less grants for the pi user — nothing else.
#
#   1. restart the pool monitor, so the deploy timer can apply updates
#      non-interactively.
#   2. run the USB recovery helper, so the monitor can re-enumerate or
#      power-cycle a wedged RTL-SDR without a person walking out to replug it.
#
# The recovery helper is deliberately the ROOT-OWNED copy in /usr/local/sbin,
# not the one the deploy syncs into ~/Desktop. Pointing sudo at a file the pi
# user can write would hand pi a general root shell; this way the privileged
# code can only change when someone with root reinstalls it (see deploy/README.md).
pi ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart pool-monitor.service, /bin/systemctl restart pool-monitor.service
pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/sdr_recovery.py
